as issues with the FOR /F eol problem. We don't want any delimiter and the =
returned string could start with any character. I couldn't figure out how t=
o use Jeb's technique of eol=3D&lt;LF&gt; in the macro.</div></blockquote><=
br><br>You simply have to insert the &lt;LF&gt; in a way, so it expand to ^=
&lt;LF&gt;&lt;LF&gt;<br><br><br><div class=3D"codebox"><p>Code: <a href=3D"=
https://www.dostips.com/forum/viewtopic.php?f=3D3&amp;t=3D1827#">Select all=
</a></p><pre><code>set lf=3D^<br><br><br>set macroToLower=3Ddo^<br>&nbsp; s=
etlocal enableDelayedExpansion^<br>&nbsp; ^&amp;set "str=3D!%%~a!"^<br>&nbs=
p; ^&amp;(for %%A in (^<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"A=3Da" "B=3Db" "C=3Dc" "D=
=3Dd" "E=3De" "F=3Df" "G=3Dg" "H=3Dh" "I=3Di"^<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; "J=3Dj" "K=
=3Dk" "L=3Dl" "M=3Dm" "N=3Dn" "O=3Do" "P=3Dp" "Q=3Dq" "R=3Dr"^<br>&nbsp; &n=
bsp; "S=3Ds" "T=3Dt" "U=3Du" "V=3Dv" "W=3Dw" "X=3Dx" "Y=3Dy" "Z=3Dz" "=C3=
=84=3D=C3=A4"^<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; "=C3=96=3D=C3=B6" "=C3=9C=3D=C3=BC"^<br>&nb=
sp; &nbsp;) do set "str=3D!str:%%~A!")^<br>&nbsp; ^&amp;(for /f ^^^"eol^^=
=3D^^^%lf%%lf%^%lf%%lf%^^ delims^^=3D^^^" %%v in ("!str!") do endlocal^&amp=
;set "%%~a=3D%%~v")<br></code></pre></div><br><br>Btw. <br>You can use also=
 the technic of the BatchLibrary prototype.<br>There I build something simi=
liar to this macro technic. <br>But instead of build the macros with many <=
strong class=3D"text-strong">&amp;</strong> I put them into brackets, then =
you can use &lt;LF&gt; to create working new lines.<br>I used this for bett=
er debugging, and it looks better  <img class=3D"smilies" src=3D"https://ww=
w.dostips.com/forum/images/smilies/icon_smile.gif" alt=3D":)" title=3D"Smil=
e"> <br><br><div class=3D"codebox"><p>Code: <a href=3D"https://www.dostips.=
com/forum/viewtopic.php?f=3D3&amp;t=3D1827#">Select all</a></p><pre><code>e=
cho off<br>setlocal disableDelayedExpansion<br><br>::----------------------=
--------------------<br>:: DEFINE MACROS<br>set lf=3D^<br><br><br>set ^"xlf=
=3D^^^%lf%%lf%^%lf%%lf%"<br>set ^"myMacro=3Ddo (%xlf%^<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;setl=
ocal enableDelayedExpansion %xlf%^<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;set ^"str=3D%%~a^"%xlf%^=
<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;echo !str!%xlf%^<br>)"<br>set "callMacro=3Dfor /f "tokens=
=3D1-26" %%a in"<br><br>:: - Test and show the code<br>echo on<br>%callMacr=
o% ("hallo") %myMacro%<br></code></pre></div><br><br><span style=3D"color: =
#40FF00">Output</span><br><div class=3D"codebox"><p>Code: <a href=3D"https:=
//www.dostips.com/forum/viewtopic.php?f=3D3&amp;t=3D1827#">Select all</a></=
p><pre><code>C:\temp&gt;for /F "tokens=3D1-26" %a in ("hallo") do (<br>setl=
ocal enableDelayedExpansion<br>&nbsp;set "str=3D%~a"<br>&nbsp;echo !str!<br=
>)<br><br>C:\temp&gt;(<br>setlocal enableDelayedExpansion<br>&nbsp;set "str=
=3Dhallo"<br>&nbsp;echo !str!<br>)<br>hallo</code></pre></div><br>jeb</div>

