he same macro. but it is quite an overhead! Or using set /p ? =3D&lt; "", b=
ut then we need a file! Also quite an overhead!<br><br>I need a brilliant t=
rick! <br></div></blockquote><br>Sorry Ed - my prior post was not in respon=
